				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aeternam75" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2236011); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2236011&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608973917" alt="aeternam75" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2236011)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aeternam75" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2236011); return false;" >aeternam75</a></span> <span class="odate time_1597839567 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Aug 2020 12:19</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4751625">
									

<p>very good tale, I really like it, I can't wait to see what follow. I have 2 critics yet, I post here (at the end of the story hopping everyone is genuine here) because I don't want it to become some kind of bait for trolls like in other place, i don't want to start a war&#8230;<br />
-I don't really understand the big emphasis on gay and trans. It's cool to have some character being like this especially when it feature so much content about freedom and modern society but I fell like it's not always relevant some character have a whole story revolving around it like bones and thus it is very relevant but some are just gay because no reason (why harmpit ? I guess they were all pre-written like this but still&#8230;) it does not add much. I fell like it's a bit like adding trans/gay for adding them without point, some character could have their sexual identity or gender not known as a part of internet anonimity (here we are sure they are not hetero), maybe it's a mean for provocation or just the way autors like it. At the end of the day if you like to wright reality-bender as gender-bender too (joke intended) I m fine with it, your story are still great. The whole emphasis on gender and non-heterosexualite in GAW is part of the GoI but I don't find it always well used or relevant.</p>
<p>Also There is no euro in Iceland they pay in krone, they accept euro in lot of places but in thoses places they also accept dollars usually&#8230; It is a bit of a plot-hole but maybe in your canon iceland is in the EU.<br />
Ps : I m terrible at english writing, I strongly identify with harmpit. I don't often comment because SCP univer is so vast that it always fell like i don't know something obvious so it is kinda intimidating, but it is possible I have skipped something that make my critic irrelevant.</p>

